# KLIC 권역별 매출 현황

Selected block: revenue-region

License index: https://design.klic.co.kr/licenses/README.md (preserve per-file notices).

Read DESIGN.md and KLIC-DESIGN-SYSTEM.json before implementation; their revision matches the API, CLI and MCP policy snapshot.

## Choosing themes, composition or source changes

- Adjust color, fonts and surfaces with supported themes and CSS tokens. Preserve klic. four-layer references, accessibility and state meaning.
- Compose workflows from existing parts and consumer-owned data, state and events. Distinguish reference HTML from standalone workspaces that include behavior.
- When internals need changes, obtain source with hashes, dependencies and licenses. Run actual appearance and source modifications in development and production, verifying images, keyboard behavior and recovery.
- Apply publishing experiments and guidance overlays only to the current session of a registered target. Do not store them in global appearance, BlockContext, business data, selection, validation or request state.
- Export supported settings through existing KLIC settings contracts. Deliver source edits separately in klic-publishing-v1 using registered targets and allowed values; reject unknown targets, properties and values.
- Exclude guides, dimension lines, selection and lesson state from product code. Generate CSS only from an allowed source recipe for a registered target.

This standalone workspace includes shared runtime files to preserve relative imports, tokens, styles and license notices. Multiple variants share source modules; it is not a minimal dependency tree.

## Run

Review source and per-file notices, then run bun install, bun run dev to preview, or bun run build to build. These commands are never executed by the KLIC CLI.

## Scope

Interactive sample data only. Connect your application's backend separately. Build output is build/. Fonts and portraits are included in public/ and copied by Vite into build/.

Reference: https://design.klic.co.kr/#blocks/revenue-region/preview
